# Cover Letter: {{COMPANY}} — {{ROLE}}

> **Length cap**: 1 page (~300-400 words).
> **Voice**: keep Nii's voice per `profile/style_guide.md`.
> **Hard rules**: never invent anything. Address gaps per match_analysis.md framings.

## Structure to produce

```markdown
# Nii Amon Dsane

[Date]

[Hiring Manager Name or "Hiring Team"]
[Title]
{{COMPANY}}

Dear [Name or "Hiring Team"],

[Paragraph 1 — Hook: 2-3 sentences. Why this company, why this role, what's the headline fit. Reference the recommended angle from match_analysis.md. If warm_intro/referral, mention the connector by name in sentence 1.]

[Paragraph 2 — Proof: 4-6 sentences. 2-3 specific outcomes from Nii's career that map directly to the JD's must-haves. Use real metrics from profile/cv.md. Lean on the roles flagged in match_analysis.md "Roles to feature prominently".]

[Paragraph 3 — Gap handling (if any gaps from match_analysis.md): 2-3 sentences. Address 1-2 most important gaps with the framing strategy from match_analysis.md. Optional — skip if no significant gaps.]

[Paragraph 4 — Close: 2 sentences. Reiterate excitement in concrete terms. Call to action (e.g., "I'd welcome a conversation about...").]

Sincerely,
Nii Amon Dsane
```

## Rules

- Do NOT use the phrase "I am writing to apply for" — overused, AI-smelling
- Do NOT use "passionate", "results-driven", "proven track record", "synergy", "leverage", "thrilled"
- Do NOT echo the JD's language word-for-word — sounds sycophantic
- DO use specific numbers from the CV
- DO reference one specific thing about the company that isn't in the JD (if known) — signals genuine interest
- DO keep sentences short (15-20 words avg)
- DO use first person, present tense for current role (Mira), past tense for prior
